4461212, "top": [[" disables", -0.3514142334461212], [" strips", -1.631279468536377]]}, {"t": " debug", "lp": -0.08481630682945251, "top": [[" debug", -0.08481630682945251], [" debugging", -3.2065908908843994]]}, {"t": " symbols", "lp": -0.31441250443458557, "top": [[" symbols", -0.31441250443458557], [" info", -1.9652494192123413]]}, {"t": ",", "lp": -0.11218993365764618, "top": [[",", -0.11218993365764618], [".", -2.826596975326538]]}, {"t": " and", "lp": -0.0017390463035553694, "top": [[" and", -0.0017390463035553694], [" enables", -8.033038139343262]]}, {"t": " enables", "lp": -1.3953840732574463, "top": [[" enables", -1.3953840732574463], [" removes", -1.948116660118103]]}, {"t": " inline", "lp": -1.89034903049469, "top": [[" in", -1.5959155559539795], [" assertions", -1.6759992837905884]]}, {"t": " functions", "lp": -0.5192651748657227, "top": [[" functions", -0.5192651748657227], [" optimizations", -2.326920509338379]]}], "text": "Here is a step-by-step, flag-by-flag explanation of the `build()` function in this PKGBUILD. This function configures and builds `llama.cpp` using Intel's oneAPI compiler suite (SYCL) for maximum performance on AMD Zen 4 CPUs and Intel Arc A770 GPUs.\n\n### 1. Environment Setup\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\nset -e\n```\n*   **`source /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force`**: Loads Intel oneAPI environment variables (paths to compilers, libraries, headers). `--force` ensures it overwrites any existing conflicting environment variables, guaranteeing a clean build environment.\n*   **`set -e`**: Causes the script to exit immediately if any command fails, preventing partial builds that could produce broken packages.\n\n### 2. CMake Configuration\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n*   **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"`**: Specifies the **source directory** (the downloaded git repo).\n*   **`-B \"${srcdir}/build\"`**: Specifies the **build directory** (where object files and intermediates go).\n*   **`-G Ninja`**: Uses **Ninja** as the build backend instead of Make. Ninja is faster for large C++ projects.\n\n### 3. Build Type & Installation Paths\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib \\\n```\n*   **`-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release`**: Enables full compiler optimizations (`-O2` or `-O3`), disables debug symbols, and enables inline functions"}